;; expect: ok
;; the checked door's limit (kernel/test/handle_test.shard): what the erasure dropped beside a
;; type's value arguments is not in the program a handle is prepared from — `small`'s evidence
;; binder, `Span`'s proposition field. Both prepare as checked entries, and each takes a value
;; its L type excludes. A load holds the environment as well, and its run (kernel/run.shard;
;; kernel/test/entry_test.shard) refuses such an entry `preconditioned` before any argument is
;; read: `guarded` for its binder, `spanned` for the field; `shown` has neither and runs
(type World (World Nat))
(structure Span () (lo Nat) (hi Nat) (ok (Nat.le lo hi)))
(fn width ((s Span)) Nat (Nat.sub (Span.hi s) (Span.lo s)))
(fn small ((n Nat) (h (Nat.lt n 10))) Nat n)
(fn shown ((n Nat) (w World)) World w)
(fn guarded ((n Nat) (h (Nat.lt n 10)) (w World)) World w)
(fn spanned ((s Span) (w World)) World w)
